==English==

===Etymology===
Onomatopoeia.

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|harrumph}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/həˈɹʌmf/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-harumph.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ha|rumph}}

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{non-gloss definition|An expression of [[disdain]], [[disbelief]], [[protest]], [[refusal]] or [[dismissal]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Harumph'''! She is welcome to try, but I'm not going to bother helping.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|expression of disbelief}} {{l|en|fiddlesticks}}, {{l|en|horsefeathers}}, {{l|en|pull the other one}}; see also [[Thesaurus:bullshit]]
* {{sense|expression of disdain}} {{l|en|feh}}, {{l|en|pfaugh}}, {{l|en|pish}}, {{l|en|pshaw}}, {{l|en|pooh}}; see also [[Thesaurus:bah]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An expression of disdain, disbelief, protest, or dismissal; a [[huff]], [[grunt]], or [[snort]].
#: ''I didn't get a '''harumph''' out of that guy.''
#: ''Give the governor a '''harumph'''.''

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To dislike, protest, or dismiss.

